Foundation post-WP-05 verification update

Stage 5 WP-05 full final validation completed successfully on governed technical baseline `fbf9b1a4c7b89efd44c3ea092ae689dac3894168`.

For FCR-0009, the bounded WP-05-owned eligibility portion is now verified satisfied:
- admitted-message expiry boundary enforced before routing;
- route-authority decision-time/expiry enforced;
- deterministic observation-time and routing identity;
- route/endpoint isolation preserved;
- no Application self-declared QoS/criticality becomes Foundation authority.

WP-05 does NOT satisfy queueing, scheduling, backpressure, flow control, latency guarantees, tail-latency measurement, delivery-hop deadline propagation, degradation execution, or delivery-outcome evidence.

`FCR_0009_WP05_PORTION = VERIFIED_SATISFIED`
`FCR_0009_OVERALL = REMAINS_OPEN_FOR_WP06_RESOURCE_OR_OBSERVABILITY_OWNERS`
`FCR_CLOSURE = NOT_YET_ELIGIBLE`

Foundation evidence: `docs/stage-5-wp05/06_FINAL_VALIDATION_AND_EVIDENCE_RECONCILIATION.md`, `07_INDEPENDENT_POST_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW.md`, and `08_FCR_AND_COMPLETENESS_RECONCILIATION.md`.

WP-06 remediation update before runtime validation

The WP-06 pressure-authority hardening identified during the fresh FCR review is now implemented.

Current WP-06-owned FCR-0009 behavior includes:
- accepted expiry/deadline preserved without hop reset;
- bounded route/producer/global pressure gating;
- governed technical traffic class with no Application self-declared Foundation criticality;
- pressure ceilings/reserve bound to explicit governed pressure authority/evidence;
- deterministic defer/degradation and delivery outcome evidence.

Status:
`FCR_0009_WP06_PRESSURE_REMEDIATION = IMPLEMENTED_PENDING_RUNTIME_VALIDATION`
`FCR_0009_OVERALL = REMAINS_OPEN`

Still outside WP-06: tail-latency aggregation/percentile observability and any Application-specific Fast-Track policy.

Current Foundation evidence: `docs/stage-5-wp06/03_REQUIREMENT_TO_VERIFIER_TRACEABILITY.md`, `04_PRE_VALIDATION_RED_TEAM_REVIEW.md`, `05_FCR_PRE_VALIDATION_DISPOSITION.md`, `06_FCR_PRE_VALIDATION_STATUS_SNAPSHOT.md`.

WP-06 focused-validation update on `foundation-development`.

Validated technical HEAD: `90112de5dc7f8b04b83f6b1b6b233e4bb92e93e2`.

WP-06-owned FCR-0009 portions now focused-runtime-verified:
- accepted expiry/deadline preserved without reset;
- bounded route/producer/global pressure gating;
- governed technical traffic priority with explicit authority;
- reserved elevated capacity without producer self-elevation;
- cross-Application pressure isolation;
- degradation/defer behavior and immutable delivery outcome timing evidence.

Evidence: `docs/stage-5-wp06/09_FOCUSED_VALIDATION_EVIDENCE.md`; WP-06 verifier `58/58 PASS` twice.

Remaining outside or after WP-06 focused validation:
- aggregate/tail-latency observability and percentile reporting;
- any broader QoS/observability capability not owned by delivery policy;
- full final Foundation regression / independent closure-readiness review;
- Application verification and final FCR reconciliation.

`FCR_OVERALL = REMAINS_OPEN`.
